			"Message": "build(Air): Commit debug and release binary artifacts via Git LFS\n\nThis commit finalizes the repository configuration for the `Air` element by enabling the tracking of pre-compiled build artifacts. This aligns with the project's strategy to use Git LFS for distributing core binaries.\n\n**Git Configuration:**\n- Updated `.gitignore` to uncomment negation patterns for `Target/debug/Air`, `Target/release/Air`, and their corresponding `libAirLibrary.rlib` static libraries. This allows Git to include these files in version control.\n\n**Artifacts Added:**\n- Added `Target/debug/Air` (debug binary)\n- Added `Target/release/Air` (release binary)\n- Added `Target/debug/libAirLibrary.rlib` (debug library)\n- Added `Target/release/libAirLibrary.rlib` (release library)\n\nThese artifacts are managed via Git LFS to ensure the repository remains performant while providing instant access to compiled versions of the `Air` background daemon.",
			"SHA": "eba857858c6cd50e57be823a7a6f8a9f960ab8dd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-03T04:51:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				128,
				29
			],
			"Message": "chore(Air): Establish project foundation with cargo config, git attributes, and licensing\n\nThis commit initializes the `Air` Element with essential project infrastructure files to support development and distribution within the Land monorepo.\n\n**Infrastructure & Build:**\n- Added `.cargo/config.toml` to define custom build targets (`Target`), optimize compiler flags (LTO, `codegen-units`, `panic=abort`), and enable specific linker optimizations for Apple Silicon (`aarch64`) and Intel (`x86_64`) Darwin targets.\n- Configured Rustdoc options for index page generation and unstable feature scraping.\n\n**Repository Hygiene:**\n- Added `.gitignore` with specific patterns for the `Target` directory, preserving built artifacts (RLIBs, EXEs, bundles) via negative lookaheads while ignoring intermediate build cruft.\n- Added `.gitattributes` to enable Git LFS for large binary artifacts (debug/release libraries and executables).\n\n**Legal & Policy:**\n- Added `LICENSE` (CC0 1.0 Universal) to define the distribution terms for the `Air` component.\n- Added `SECURITY.md` outlining the vulnerability reporting process, supported versions, and security policies specific to the Land ecosystem.\n- Added `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` based on the Contributor Covenant 2.1 to foster a safe and inclusive community.\n- Added `CHANGELOG.md` initialized for version `0.0.1`.\n\n**gRPC & Protocol:**\n- Reformatted `Proto/Air.proto` to strictly use 2-space indentation, improving consistency across the protocol definition for the `AirService`.\n\n**Build System:**\n- Updated `build.rs` to remove the unused `std::io::Result` import, silence `non_snake_case` warnings for generated code, and ensure the proto file change triggers a rebuild.\n\n**Source Updates:**\n- Adjusted `Source/Vine/Server/AirVinegRPCService.rs` to derive `Clone` for the gRPC service struct, necessary for sharing across asynchronous tasks in the server lifecycle.\n- Minor formatting adjustments across `Source/Indexing` and `Source/*` modules to align with the new `Cargo.toml` linter settings (e.g., spacing in generic arguments).\n\nThis creates a robust foundation for the `Air` background daemon, ensuring proper artifact management, clear legal standing, and optimized compilation.",
			"SHA": "93cff0e6a05c993d41c19145558225d7801747ec"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-03T02:04:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				124,
				30
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Air): Enforce PascalCase naming conventions and correct module visibility\n\nThis commit enforces strict PascalCase naming for all struct fields and public identifiers across the Air codebase, aligning with the broader Land ecosystem's architectural standards (Mountain, Wind, Cocoon). It also corrects module visibility and resolves compilation errors introduced by previous refactors.\n\n**Struct Field Renaming:**\n- Updated all public struct fields in `AirConfiguration`, `RetryPolicy`, `CircuitBreakerConfig`, `RetryEvent`, `CircuitStatistics`, `BulkheadStatistics`, and `Metrics` to use PascalCase (e.g., `memory_usage_mb` -> `MemoryUsageMb`, `max_retries` -> `MaxRetries`).\n- Updated generated gRPC message field access to match the new casing (e.g., `request_id`, `username`).\n\n**Module Structure & Visibility:**\n- Refactored the `Indexing` module hierarchy: `Indexing/mod.rs` no longer re-exports submodules inline. Submodules (`State`, `Scan`, `Process`, etc.) are now declared as `pub mod` to allow external access, while internal logic resolves types via absolute paths (`crate::Indexing::...`).\n- Removed extensive module-level documentation in favor of file-based organization, cleaning up `mod.rs` files in `Background`, `Language`, `Scan`, `Store`, and `Watch`.\n- Consolidated re-exports of types like `FileIndex`, `SymbolInfo` in `Indexing/mod.rs` to simplify dependencies.\n\n**gRPC & Proto Updates:**\n- Renamed the generated gRPC module `Air` to `air` (lowercase) in `Vine/Generated/mod.rs` and updated imports in `AirVinegRPCService.rs` to match `tonic`'s expected casing for generated packages.\n\n**Configuration & Logic Fixes:**\n- Added `MaxParallelIndexing` configuration to `IndexingConfig` with a default value.\n- Fixed function calls in `ConfigurationManager` to use PascalCase property accessors.\n- Corrected `Clone` implementations in `DownloadManager`, `CircuitBreaker`, `BulkheadExecutor`, and `ResilienceOrchestrator` to reference renamed fields.\n- Updated `UpdateManager` and `AirVinegRPCService` to use PascalCase properties from `AppState` and configuration structs (e.g., `Enabled`, `Channel`).\n- Fixed method calls in `PluginManager` (`CheckAirVersionCompatibility` -> `version_satisfies`) to resolve private method visibility issues.\n\nThese changes ensure type consistency across Rust and TypeScript boundaries, improve code readability, and fix compilation errors related to casing mismatches and module privacy.",
			"SHA": "7bed9f7736dcae090318f0d702685ad8fde48eec"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-02T11:51:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠁⠀⠀",
				124,
				52
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Air): Rename binary to 'Air' and update naming conventions\n\nThis commit standardizes the capitalization of the Air project's binary and naming conventions, shifting from lowercase 'air' to PascalCase 'Air'. This aligns with the broader Land ecosystem's styling (e.g., Mountain, Wind, Cocoon) and ensures consistency across CLI usage, configuration paths, logging, and documentation.\n\nKey changes include:\n\n- **Binary Rename**: The executable and command references are now `Air` instead of `air`. This affects CLI parsing, help messages, and shell commands.\n- **Configuration Paths**: Default paths now use `~/.Air/`, `/etc/Air/`, and `Air.toml` instead of `~/.air/`, `/etc/air/`, and `air.toml`.\n- **gRPC Protocol**: The protobuf package name is updated from `air` to `Air`. Consequently, the generated gRPC service paths now use `Air.AirService`.\n- **Code Generation**: Removed `Source/Vine/Generated/Air.rs` and consolidated generated code to follow the new package casing.\n- **Documentation**: `README.md` diagrams and `CONTRIBUTING.md` now reflect the updated naming.\n- **Log and File Naming**: Log prefixes and file names (e.g., `Air.log`) and directories (e.g., `/var/log/Air`) use the new casing.\n\nThis refactor improves project branding clarity and reduces ambiguity regarding the daemon's identity within the Land architecture.",
			"SHA": "c023dedf221dc58de9c2b026d90d1d487a04b190"
		},
